From a742401dc2fb566c8c42f84542a26ffb89b67bad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crit-Fumble <noreply@crit-fumble.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:47:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chore(deps): refresh the lockfile for the multer,
 body-parser, undici and proxy-addr advisories

`npm audit fix --package-lock-only --omit=dev`, inside the ranges package.json
already allows; package.json is unchanged. It moves:

- multer 2.2.0 -> 2.5.0 (GHSA-q7qp-rjg7-q26m, GHSA-qfvm-cv95-jqjf)
- body-parser 2.3.0 -> 2.4.0 (GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828)
- proxy-addr 2.0.7 -> 2.0.8 (GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h)
- undici 7.29.0 -> 7.30.1, axios 1.19.0 -> 1.21.0, follow-redirects
  1.16.0 -> 1.16.2, fast-uri 3.1.5 -> 3.1.9, image-size 2.0.2 -> 2.0.4,
  probe-image-size 7.3.0 -> 7.5.0, nodemailer 9.0.5 -> 9.1.1
- and their own dependencies (content-type, morgan, qs); probe-image-size 7.5
  no longer pulls stream-parser and its readable-stream chain.

These are the versions master's lockfile already carries, except nodemailer,
whose fix is a major version outside the ^9.0.5 range. The patch-package
patch for body-parser applies unchanged, as it does on master.
